File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-neon-abi-and-enforcer.oot
Status: open — audit snapshot 2026-08-26.
Context: Read-only audit. No .oo files were modified by this audit itself.

---

## 1. New V0-V31 NEON AAPCS64 helpers

The file `ooda/std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo` grew from 97 lines to 162 lines after
the addition of eight new public functions. Each function is a pure constant per the
existing 4-element Academy header.

| #  | Function                          | Register file          | AAPCS64 rule                            |
|----|-----------------------------------|------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
|  1 | abi_fp_arg_count()                | V0-V7                  | Eight FP/vector argument slots.         |
|  2 | abi_fp_arg_reg(i)                 | V0-V7                  | Clamp i to the 0..7 range.              |
|  3 | abi_fp_ret_reg()                  | V0                     | Primary FP/vector return.               |
|  4 | abi_fp_ret_hi_reg()               | V1                     | High half of 128-bit return.            |
|  5 | abi_is_fp_arg_reg(reg)            | V0-V7                  | Argument register predicate.            |
|  6 | abi_is_fp_callee_saved(reg)       | V16-V31                | Upper NEON file is callee-saved.        |
|  7 | abi_valid_fp_reg(reg)             | V0-V31                 | Range predicate for the FP file.        |
|  8 | abi_fp_indirect_result_reg()      | V8                     | AAPCS64 indirect-result location.       |

The full callee-saved set is now: integer X19-X28 plus FP/LR X29-X30, and NEON V16-V31.
V0-V7 are caller-saved (arguments and scratch). V8-V15 are caller-saved (lower NEON
and indirect result). V16-V31 are callee-saved (upper NEON). The 16-byte stack
alignment helper stays at `abi_stack_aligned(size)`.

## 2. Type-annotation repairs

Two files had `let` statements missing the mandatory type annotation required by
QUICKREF §1.4 (Mandatory Type Annotation Law). Both repairs restored the type
annotations and kept the file under the 256-line cap.

### 2.1 oodac/aarch64_emit_alu.oo

| Line | Old binding                       | New binding                |
|------|-----------------------------------|----------------------------|
|  22  | let n = bytes_len(s);             | let n: Int = bytes_len(s); |
|  24  | let mut i = 0;                    | let mut i: Int = 0;        |
|  25  | let mut neg = false;              | let mut neg: Bool = false; |
|  28  | let v = a64_int_digits(...);      | let v: Int = a64_int_digits(...); |
|  30  | let mut acc = v;                  | let mut acc: Int = v;      |
|  75  | let mut e = p + 1 + ...;          | let mut e: Int = ...;      |
| 114  | let p = j + list_get(w, 0);       | let p: Int = ...;          |
| 132  | let mut e = p + 1 + ...;          | let mut e: Int = ...;      |
| 161  | let n = list_len(toks);           | let n: Int = list_len(toks); |
| 163  | let mut i = 0;                    | let mut i: Int = 0;        |
| 166  | let p = i + 2;                    | let p: Int = i + 2;        |
| 168  | let mut q = p + 5;                | let mut q: Int = p + 5;    |
| 169  | let mut neg = false;              | let mut neg: Bool = false; |
| 176  | let mut acc_v = a_v;              | let mut acc_v: Int = a_v;  |

The repair also added the missing `import "aarch64_emit_int.oo";` at line 17 so
the call to `aarch64_emit_int_write(folded)` resolves. File stayed at 206 lines.

