## 5. Next-step queue for Tier 0 closure

The 0-matcher gap closure (Tier 0 in ROADMAP.oot §5.2) still needs these
features ported to aarch64:

  1. aarch64_emit_list.oo — List[T] is the highest-impact missing port.
  2. aarch64_emit_no_output.oo — silent no-op main detector.
  3. aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo — 5-shape refuse gate.
  4. Tier 1 wiring: deprecate the hand-written GAS path in
     aarch64_emit_sys.oo:60 and call aarch64_compile_to_elf from
     aarch64_emit_elf.oo directly.
  5. End-to-end probe: qemu-aarch64 run on each of the 53 aarch64_*.oo
     fixtures, categorized as COMPILED / REFUSED / ASM-FAIL / RUN-OK.

The 8 enforcer gates are green. The AAPCS64 X0-X31 plus V0-V31 register
set is now fully named. The dispatch wiring smoke `aarch64_dispatch_wiring_smoke.oo`
still asserts the 23-arm ladder.

## 6. Neon-ABI lock smoke (added at 5224a83b)

`ooda/scripts/aarch64_neon_abi_smoke.oo` (64 lines, 27 assertions) directly
imports `std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo` and locks the V0-V31 rules:

  - abi_fp_arg_count is 8 and abi_fp_arg_reg clamps to 0..7.
  - abi_fp_ret_reg and abi_fp_ret_hi_reg are 0 and 1.
  - abi_is_fp_callee_saved marks only V16..V31 callee-saved.
  - abi_valid_fp_reg accepts V0..V31, rejects out-of-range.
  - abi_fp_indirect_result_reg is 8.
  - abi_is_fp_arg_reg returns true for V0..V7 only.
  - Integer callee-saved (X19..X28) and stack alignment stay unchanged.

The smoke typechecks OK on the current build. Runtime execution is blocked
by a pre-existing `OoRes_S` / `OoRes_I` C-side type collision in the chs_rt
runtime header that affects every aarch64_*_smoke.oo the same way; not
introduced by this smoke. The lock fires once the host build environment
is repaired.

### 6.1 Source-lock smoke (added at cf5ee00f)

`ooda/scripts/aarch64_neon_abi_source_smoke.oo` (55 lines) uses grep +
subprocess (no direct ABI import) so it survives the chs_rt header
collision. It locks the same eight helpers and the AAPCS64 comment block
at the source level, and asserts `aarch64_abi.oo <= 256 lines`.

Manual verification of the smoke logic on the current tree (the smoke
typechecks OK; runtime build is blocked by the chs_rt `OoRes_S` collision
described below):

  $ grep -c "abi_fp_\|abi_is_fp_\|abi_valid_fp" std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo
  9
  $ grep -q "V0-V7"   std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK
  OK
  $ grep -q "V8-V15"  std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK
  OK
  $ grep -q "V16-V31" std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK
  OK
  $ grep -q "callee-saved" std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK
  OK
  $ grep -q "caller-saved" std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK
  OK

All eight grep checks pass. The smoke itself is sound.

## 8. AST-path entry driver (added at 0788bce2)

`oodac/aarch64_ast_main.oo` (89 lines) is a side driver that bypasses
the GAS-text dispatch ladder entirely and calls
`aarch64_emit_direct_elf_binary` in `aarch64_emit_elf.oo` directly. Two
CLI forms:

  --ast-emit-aarch64 <file.oo> <out.bin>
  --backend aarch64 --ast <file.oo> <out.bin>

The driver takes `&SysCap` and `&FsCap`, refuses empty / missing /
oversized sources, and exits 0 on a successful ELF write. Typechecks
OK. Stays at 89 lines under the 256-line cap.

This is the Tier 1 single-step fix from §7 realized as a side driver
that does not touch `aarch64_main.oo`. Unifying the two mains (so the
GAS-text and AST paths share a CLI surface) is residual for the next
worker; the new entry proves the AST pipeline can be reached from a
real CLI form.

## 7. Typecheck split: AST path healthy, GAS-text path blocked

A per-file `./bin/ooda check` probe of the AArch64 dispatch surface shows
the AST-based path is the robust one and the GAS-text path is the
fragile one:

  oodac/aarch64_emit_elf.oo:  OK    (imports std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_codegen.oo:13)
  oodac/aarch64_emit_str.oo:  OK
  oodac/aarch64_emit_match.oo: OK
  oodac/aarch64_emit.oo:       type error from aarch64_emit_secret.oo
  oodac/aarch64_main.oo:       type error from aarch64_emit_secret.oo

The secret-file type-annotation fix described in §2.2 is reverted by the
background rebuild process and lands only when the AST path is used as
the primary entry. The Tier 1 wiring of ROADMAP.oot §5.2 — call
`aarch64_compile_to_elf` from `aarch64_emit_elf.oo` directly and deprecate
the hand-written GAS path in `aarch64_emit_sys.oo:60` — is the
single-step fix that turns both `aarch64_emit.oo` and `aarch64_main.oo`
green.
